==English==
{{Webster 1913}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|formula|ate|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|formulates|formulating|formulated}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=en}} To reduce to, or express in, a formula; to put in a clear and definite form of statement or expression.<!-- G. P. Marsh. -->
#* {{quote-book|year=1988|author=Andrew Radford|title=Transformational Grammar|location=Cambridge|publisher=University Press|page=19|isbn=0-521-34750-5}}
#*: Another source of evidence supporting the conclusion that children learn language by '''formulating''' a set of rules comes from the ''errors'' that they produce. A case in point are overgeneralized past tense forms like ''comed'', ''goed'', ''seed'', ''buyed'', ''bringed'', etc. frequently used by young children. [...]

